course: dictionary
lesson: 6303
title: Morning: a time of day
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Morning» is a time label. It splits the day into parts, like afternoon and evening. Look at the words around it: «in the morning», «this morning» and «Sunday mornings» all tell you when something happens.
explain: «His dad plays a fighting game with him on Sunday mornings, sitting right next to him.» The words «on Sunday» and «sitting right next to him» help you see that morning means the early part of the day, not a whole day. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: «The train leaves at 2 o'clock in the morning.» Here morning means the time from midnight to noon. This is a second meaning, so the clock time tells you which meaning the writer means.
fact: Morning is a noun, and its plural is mornings.
fact: «Morning» means the early part of the day, from when the sun rises until midday (noon).
fact: «Morning» can also mean the time from midnight to noon, as in «2 o'clock in the morning».
fact: «Good morning» is a greeting you say when you meet someone in the morning.
fact: «Morning tea» is a short break with a snack or drink in the morning, used in Britain and Australia.
exercise: «His dad plays a fighting game with him on Sunday mornings.» What does morning mean here? | A kind of breakfast cereal | *The early part of the day, from sunrise until midday | Midnight only | The evening after tea
exercise: «Good morning, class!» What is «Good morning» used for? | A goodbye at bedtime | *A greeting you say when you meet someone | A question about the time
exercise: «One morning she nearly stepped in front of a van.» Mia says morning means after lunch. What does morning mean? | The time just after sunset | The whole of Monday | The time after lunch until bedtime | *The early part of the day, from sunrise until midday
test: «2 o'clock in the morning» shows that morning can mean what? | The time from noon to midnight | Only the moment the sun rises | A type of bus | *The time from midnight to noon
test: «Breath smells in the morning because germs grow overnight.» Which part of the day is the morning? | The night before | The whole week | The afternoon | *The early part, from sunrise until midday
exam: Which sentence uses morning for the time from midnight to noon? | «Good morning, everyone!» | «We ate our supper in the evening.» | «The sun sets in the west.» | *«The train leaves at 2 o'clock in the morning.»
